                <pb facs="0138" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894c.111/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-07T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>268. Referring to Department’s despatch No. 18 of June 24, 1920, concerning
                    temporary war-time passport control on the Japanese and Russian railways please
                    telegraph result of your conferences with your colleagues in the premises.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
